s-authoring priority exception, E002 inherits P2 from the strategy's `priority: Normal` frontmatter rather than pushing priority upstream. |\n44\t\n45\tNo other edges: E001 is the only code Implementation epic (single component,\n46\tsingle team, one logical change — two report surfaces in the same console with\n47\tthe same work-product type), so there is nothing to parallelize or serialize\n48\tagainst it. No Investigation epics exist (see below).\n49\t\n50\t## Component Mapping\n51\t\n52\tStrategy component names mapped to canonical RHAI Jira components\n53\t(`.context/rhai-components.txt`):\n54\t\n55\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Classification |\n56\t|--------------------|---------------------|----------------|\n57\t| RHOAI web console | Dashboard | Active — code changes (both reports, CSV export) |\n58\t| Notebook controller | Notebooks | Passive — existing activity-tracking data source; no code changes |\n59\t| Kubeflow Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | Passive — existing run-metadata data source; no code changes |\n60\t\n61\tAll three components exist in `.context/architecture-context/`\n62\t(`dashboard.md`, `notebooks.md`, `data-science-pipelines.md`), so no new\n63\tcomponent was detected and no onboarding chain (repo/license/Konflux) is\n64\tneeded. The Dashboard is already Konflux-onboarded per its context file, and no\n65\t`konflux-onboarding` epic exists in this decomposition.\n66\t\n67\tPassive components: the same consuming team (RHOAI Dashboard) validates both\n68\tdata sources, so per Step 2 no separate validation epics are generated —\n69\tvalidation is folded into E001's acceptance criteria (report values must\n70\treconcile with the notebook controller's activity tracking and Kubeflow\n71\tPipelines run metadata).\n72\t\n73\t## Investigation Epics\n74\t\n75\tNone. The strategy's Open Questions section is explicitly \"None\", and there\n76\tare no risks, assumptions-with-conditions, pending reviews, or conditional\n77\tADRs. Th