8\t  Documentation). Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs rather\n109\t  than strategy-level ACs.\n110\t- **Scope trap watch (non-blocking)**: the stale-run report's \"retained\n111\t  artifacts\" column implies artifact storage metadata is reachable from run\n112\t  metadata; if artifact listing proves expensive at scale, the implementing\n113\t  team should degrade gracefully rather than expanding scope into storage\n114\t  management (which the strategy's out-of-scope boundaries — no automated\n115\t  reclamation — support keeping out).\n116\t- No priority inversions detected: the only cross-epic priority difference\n117\t  (E001 P1 → E002 P2) is the intended docs-authoring exception, and E002 does\n118\t  not block any P0/P1 work.\n119\t\n120\t## Tiered Delivery\n121\t\n122\tNot applicable. There are no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all\n123\tdata sources are in-platform and GA per architecture context.\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d6bbcb4741d5ff8","agent_id":"a20d059811d41b568","session_id":"270e0692-b5f6-41dc-9064-3e5481aa32f8","uuid":"18b4bae0-6114-4eff-80e3-b5a6d23161ea","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:22:55.705Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-beabf1872e9d1ddb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
