{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97556515bac39508","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers two administrator-facing reports in the RHOAI web console:\n34\ta per-project idle-workbench report and a stale pipeline-run report, each\n35\texportable as CSV. Both reports are read-only views over data that already\n36\texists in the platform — the notebook controller's activity tracking and\n37\tKubeflow Pipelines run metadata — so no changes are made to those components;\n38\tthe console work is purely surfacing the data.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Per-project idle-workbench report in the web console showing, for each\n43\t  workbench, its last activity, owner, and reserved resources, sourced from\n44\t  the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n45\t- Stale pipeline-run report in the web console showing completed pipeline\n46\t  runs older than a configurable age that have retained artifacts, sourced\n47\t  from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n48\t- The configurable age threshold for the stale pipeline-run report.\n49\t- CSV export of either report, available to administrators, containing the\n50\t  same rows and columns as the on-screen report.\n51\t- Read-only reporting only — automated reclamation/deletion of idle resources\n52\t  and cost/chargeback calculations are out of scope per the strategy.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given a project containing workbenches with differing last-activity times,\n57\t  the console displays a per-project report listing each workbench's last\n58\t  activity, owner, and reserved resources, and the values reconcile with the\n59\t  notebook controller's activity-tracking data (passive-component validation).\n60\t- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs of differing ages, the\n61\t  console displays a report listing the completed runs older than the\n62\t  configured age along with their retained artifacts, and the values\n63\t  reconcile with Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata (passive-component\n64\t  validation).\n65\t- The age threshold for the stale pipeline-run report is configurable and the\n66\t  report reflects changes to it.\n67\t- An administrator can export either report as CSV, and the CSV contains the\n68\t  same rows and columns as the on-screen report.\n69\t- No code changes are required in the notebook controller or Kubeflow\n70\t  Pipelines; both are consumed strictly as existing data sources.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n75\t  reserved resources) sourced from notebook-controller activity tracking.\n76\t- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n77\t  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n78\t  run metadata.\n79\t- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report. Bundled because the\n80\t  export renders the same report surfaces HLR-1 and HLR-2 build — it shares\n81\t  their rows and columns and has no standalone surface, so it is not\n82\t  separately schedulable as its own epic.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d6bbcb4741d5ff8","agent_id":"a20d059811d41b568","session_id":"270e0692-b5f6-41dc-9064-3e5481aa32f8","uuid":"9dedb305-c03e-40de-92f9-90679b72b94b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:22:57.780Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-97556515bac39508","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
