trator can take for\n51\t  resources identified as idle or stale — manual, administrator-driven steps\n52\t  only. Automated reclamation/deletion and cost/chargeback calculations are\n53\t  out of scope per the strategy and must not be documented as features.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Published documentation explains both reports, including every column each\n58\t  report displays, the data source behind each, and the CSV export action.\n59\t- Published documentation explains how to configure the stale-run age\n60\t  threshold.\n61\t- Published documentation describes safe, manual reclamation steps consistent\n62\t  with the strategy's out-of-scope boundaries (no automated reclamation, no\n63\t  cost/chargeback).\n64\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented console\n65\t  reports so that documented columns, configuration, and behavior match what\n66\t  shipped.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d6bbcb4741d5ff8","agent_id":"a20d059811d41b568","session_id":"270e0692-b5f6-41dc-9064-3e5481aa32f8","uuid":"544cff10-0605-4bed-a2f6-bb3923ae5da6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:22:58.476Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aec2be1aa2fd0419","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
