equired by HLR-4 and a docs-authoring epic\n102\texists, satisfying Rule 11. Strategy-level context handling is appropriate:\n103\tOpen Questions is \"None\", and the missing strategy sections (no Impacted Teams,\n104\tDependencies, ACs, NFRs) are recorded in Health Warnings rather than silently\n105\tdropped, with owner teams inferred from architecture context and ACs derived\n106\tfrom the HLRs.\n107\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b148845b6518ca06","agent_id":"ac4cac1f388da34dc","session_id":"270e0692-b5f6-41dc-9064-3e5481aa32f8","uuid":"79e9aa83-2702-43c2-af11-350bd65d0229","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:25:00.536Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5ee676b69507259","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
